# Real security fix (2026-08-20): `vercel --prod` from the CLI uploads the
# local working directory as-is — it does NOT respect .gitignore. Every
# manual deploy this project has ever made bundled the real local `.env`
# (real OAuth secrets, API keys) straight into the deployment artifact,
# where pydantic-settings' dotenv loader picked it up silently — that's
# why Basecamp OAuth "worked" in production despite never having its
# credentials set as real Vercel environment variables. Never remove this
# line; all real secrets belong in Vercel env vars (`vercel env add`),
# never in a file that gets uploaded.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.example.python

# Local-only artifacts, never needed in the deployed function.
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
node_modules/
